<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Generated: four identical slots with distinct ids.

  RemoteViews cannot reuse one <include> with different ids, so the slots are
  spelled out rather than shared. Each can render either as a headline stat
  (header + value + sub) or as a table (header + rows), and the provider hides
  whichever parts that block does not use — which is what lets a student put
  attendance, classes held and today's timetable in whatever order they want
  inside a single widget.

  Colours and typefaces are deliberately absent here. Every TextView is
  coloured and typefaced by the provider from the student's chosen theme,
  because a colour baked into this file cannot follow a palette change and was
  the reason section headers used to render grey-on-orange.
-->
